  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NURTURE-Zimbabwe: Neotree-enabled Newborn Care Research, Technology, Understanding, and Resource and Community Engagement</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is an 18-month programme supported by the UK Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office and undertaken in collaboration with University College London and the Biomedical Research And Training Institute in Zimbabwe. The purpose of this programme is to test Neotree&apos;s quality-improvement platform at a greater scale to better understand its impact on newborn deaths, and internationally defined measures of quality of care. This will involve work to substantially improve the functionality of Neotree and capacity building work in quality improvement knowledge and skills through a UK-Zimbabwe Quality Improvement programme. Neotree will use these activities and outputs to deliver a business case/ plan for larger scale-up of Neotree across Zimbabwe.</narrative>
  </description>
